<<<BEGIN PATCH>>>
From 2a11f8ee42b758147e0243595dacfc74298d41b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 13:00:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Refactor combat to KeywordEffects registry, switch to
 STS-style economy

- Extract scattered keyword switch statements (Combat.gd, Card.gd) into a
  single KeywordEffects autoload. Adding a new keyword now means editing
  one file: register display text + on_play / on_death hooks. Combat.gd
  exposes draw_one / damage_player_hero / damage_enemy_hero / get_opposing_card
  as the narrow surface the registry mutates.
- Mana is now a fixed pool of 3 refilled each turn, with chronograph/ash_crown
  relics adding +1 in their own scopes. Hand draw moves to draw-5-at-start
  and discard-hand-at-end of turn (Slay-the-Spire pattern). Enemy mana scales
  modestly with turn number to match the lower cost curve.
- Rescale every card's cost into the 1..3 range so the new mana pool is
  meaningful. ATK/HP unchanged.
- Add deck view + once-per-run card-removal events to MapView. Players can
  open their full deck at any time and spend a removal token to thin it.
- Wire MetaState.unlocked_cards into CardDB pools: tier-3 cards are now
  locked by default and unlocked one at a time on each victory. MainMenu
  shows unlock progress; GameOver announces the new unlock.
- Move phoenix_heart_consumed from per-fight Combat state to RunState so the
  relic correctly persists across combats within a run.
